# Byte-preservation DoD (plan §5.3 / M2): after supersede, the OLD ADR
# differs from its original bytes in ONLY the status line (accepted ->
# superseded) and a single inserted superseded-by line. Asserted mechanically
# by comparing the whole file against a want-fixture that is byte-identical
# except for those two lines — the body, all other frontmatter, blank lines,
# and even the trailing newline must be preserved exactly.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exec constitution supersede ADR-0001 --title 'Replacement rule' --body-file body.md
stdout 'superseded ADR-0001'

# The whole old file, byte-for-byte, equals the original with only the two
# intended line changes.
cmp constitution/adr/ADR-0001-original-rule.md want-old-adr.md

-- constitution.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
consent:
  policy: off
sourceTracking:
  type: none
categories:
  - architecture

-- constitution/adr/ADR-0001-original-rule.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: Original rule
category: architecture
date: 2026-06-01
status: accepted
---

## Context and Problem Statement

The original context, with specific   spacing   and punctuation: kept!

## Considered Options

- Option A
- Option B

## Decision Outcome

The original decision, frozen forever.

-- want-old-adr.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: Original rule
category: architecture
date: 2026-06-01
status: superseded
superseded-by: ADR-0002
---

## Context and Problem Statement

The original context, with specific   spacing   and punctuation: kept!

## Considered Options

- Option A
- Option B

## Decision Outcome

The original decision, frozen forever.

-- body.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

Replacement context.

## Considered Options

- Keep
- Replace

## Decision Outcome

Replace the original rule.
